<section class="block downscale-diagnostics">
  <h2>Downscale diagnostics</h2>
  <div class="subhead">
    Sanity checks on how parent (district) predictions were disaggregated to
    children. A high zone-0 count or many uniform-split parents means child
    zone classification is largely not data-driven — see acestor issue #49.
  </div>
  <ul>
    <li>Conservation max abs err: {{ "%.3g"|format(downscale_diagnostics.conservation_max_abs_err or 0.0) }}</li>
    <li>Parents split uniformly (no-data fallback): {{ downscale_diagnostics.n_parents_uniform or 0 }}</li>
    <li>Parent-vs-child zones — children above parent: {{ downscale_diagnostics.n_weeks_children_above_parent or 0 }}; below: {{ downscale_diagnostics.n_weeks_children_below_parent or 0 }}</li>
    <li>Children carrying zone-0 sentinel: {{ downscale_diagnostics.n_zone_zero or 0 }} / {{ downscale_diagnostics.n_total or 0 }}</li>
  </ul>
</section>
